        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/a9a28c/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2011-12-02T07:13:41.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Yes I know there’s an errata, that’s not what the topic is about  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/stuck_out_tongue.png?v=12\" title=\":stuck_out_tongue:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":stuck_out_tongue:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Play this card next to a Target, other than the Villain Character Card. Whenever that target deals damage, you may redirect that damage to another target. If you do, The Visionary deals 3 psychic damage to that target and 3 psychic damage to herself.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If the target leaves play, destroy this card.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>My confusion is which target is “that target”.</p>\n<p>Say you have Visionary, a Kraken, and Citizen Dawn out.     Wrest the Mind played on the Kraken.</p>\n<p>Environment turn rolls around, which of the following is correct?</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Visionary deals 3 damage to herself, and redirects the Krakens attack towards Dawn, dealing her 5 damage.   The Kraken then takes 3 damage from Wrest the Mind.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Visionary deals 3 damage to herself and redirects the Krakens attack towards Dawn, dealing her 5 damage.   Dawn then takes an additional 3 damage from Wrest the Mind.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>I’ve been playing 1,   but I can definitely see a case for 2.   Either way I feel is an acceptable reading of the text.<br>\nthanks for any clarification<br>\n-awp</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:34:59.607Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
