        "raw": "Yes I know there's an errata, that's not what the topic is about  :P\n\n\n\n> Play this card next to a Target, other than the Villain Character Card. Whenever that target deals damage, you may redirect that damage to another target. If you do, The Visionary deals 3 psychic damage to that target and 3 psychic damage to herself.\n\n> If the target leaves play, destroy this card.\n\n\nMy confusion is which target is \"that target\".   \n\nSay you have Visionary, a Kraken, and Citizen Dawn out.     Wrest the Mind played on the Kraken.\n\nEnvironment turn rolls around, which of the following is correct?\n\n1.   Visionary deals 3 damage to herself, and redirects the Krakens attack towards Dawn, dealing her 5 damage.   The Kraken then takes 3 damage from Wrest the Mind.\n\n2.   Visionary deals 3 damage to herself and redirects the Krakens attack towards Dawn, dealing her 5 damage.   Dawn then takes an additional 3 damage from Wrest the Mind.\n\nI've been playing 1,   but I can definitely see a case for 2.   Either way I feel is an acceptable reading of the text.\nthanks for any clarification\n-awp",
